Shipped in b8e2437. Fires exactly once across ../casey_ai: api/solver/window.py:132, the known defect.

One design decision was added during implementation that the issue did not anticipate. A first run against casey_ai produced 13 fires, 12 of them false positives in the test tree -- frozen-clock fakes shaped as:

    class _FrozenNow(datetime):
        @classmethod
        def now(cls, tz: tzinfo | None = None) -> datetime: ...

datetime.now, fromtimestamp and astimezone all take tzinfo | None in the stdlib, so an override cannot narrow to ZoneInfo without failing the type checker. Everything inside a class whose bases include datetime is now exempt. Alternatives weighed: exempting by method name (now/fromtimestamp/astimezone) would also cover Protocol-based clock fakes but passes any unrelated method called 'now'; requiring both conditions would fire on a Protocol clock fake that has no clean fix. The base-class test was chosen as the narrowest thing covering all 12.
